Hi,
We've apparently managed to out-release the ACPI codebase. Good.
The changes are as follows:

Version 0.26
        Sanitize the /proc/acpi/asus/info output, add SFUN to be handled by
                userspace
        React politely to acpi=off
        Corrected printk prefixes
        Marked functions with __init and __exit, in-kernel module size
		reduced by a whopping 500 bytes
        Fixed a long-standing typo that prevented reading WLED state
        Added support for L5830 (aka L5C)
        Call BSTS at init to reenable hotkeys for L2000E

There is only one patch both for 2.4 and 2.6, with a minor offset for the
latter:
http://hell.org.pl/~sziwan/asus/acpi4asus-0.25-0.26.diff 

Please apply.

Note: the sourceforge project release will be out once I have the docs
updated, which might take a day or two.

